User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"If you haven’t already, check out our [contributing guidelines](https://github.com/Expensify/ReactNativeChat/blob/main/contributingGuides/CONTRIBUTING.md) for onboarding and email contributors@expensify.com to request to join our Slack channel!\n___\n\n**Version Number:** v9.3.91-0\n**Reproducible in staging?:** Yes\n**Reproducible in production?:** Yes\n**If this was caught during regression testing, add the test name, ID and link from BrowserStack:** https://test-management.browserstack.com/projects/2219752/test-runs/TR-37256/folder/13176924/41237571/1455625236?sort=%2Bstatus_id\n**Email or phone of affected tester (no customers):** gocemate+b215490617@gmail.com\n**Issue reported by:** Applause Internal Team\n**Bug source:** Exploratory - Significant User Experience Deterioration\n**Device used:** Windows 10/Chrome\n**App Component:** Other\n\n## Action Performed:\n1. Sign up with a account with the following format: [anything]@tstsg.com e.g: isagoicotest@tstsg.com\n2. Verify the first modal for the onboarding flow is \"What's your name\" modal\n3. Fill in the required personal details (First Name, Last Name) and continue\n4. Verify that the next screen is the \"People you may know are already here! Verify your email to join them.\" step, prompting the user to confirm their email \n5. Select the \"Skip\" option on the verification screen.\n6. Verify that the flow proceeds to the \"What do you want to do today? step\n7. Select the \"Manage expenses for employees\", > \"5-10 employees\" option and complete the process\n8. Navigate to #admins\n9. Select any of Concierge options\n10. Verify that Concierge provide an answer\n11. Wait for the new Concierge options\n\n## Expected Result:\nConcierge questions should not load long every time\n\n## Actual Result:\nConcierge questions  loads long every time\n\n## Workaround:\nUnknown\n\n## Platforms:\n- [ ] Android: App\n- [ ] Android: mWeb Chrome\n- [ ] iOS: App\n- [ ] iOS: mWeb Safari\n- [ ] iOS: mWeb Chrome\n- [x] Windows: Chrome\n- [ ] MacOS: Chrome Safari\n\n## Screenshots/Videos\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/74ccc7db-1a37-4e29-95cd-cbe9664e967c\n\n[View all open jobs on GitHub](https://github.com/Expensify/App/issues?q=is%3Aopen+is%3Aissue+label%3A%22Help+Wanted%22)\n\n\n> **Applause Internal Information**\n> Exported by: Svetlana Lazutkina\n> Bug ID: 7169516\n<details><summary>Upwork Automation - Do Not Edit</summary>\n    <ul>\n        <li>Upwork Job URL: <a href=\"https://www.upwork.com/jobs/~022061798385854101836\">https://www.upwork.com/jobs/~022061798385854101836</a></li>\n        <li>Upwork Job ID: 2061798385854101836</li>\n        <li>Last Price Increase: 2026-06-09</li>\n    </ul>\n</details>\n\n<details><summary>Issue Owner</summary>Current Issue Owner: @s77rt</details>","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Expensify/App/issues/92364/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Expensify/App/issues/92364/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"reopened","pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/71","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/71/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/71/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/71/events","html_url":"https://github.com/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/71","id":3904303864,"node_id":"I_kwDORGgqa87otvL4","number":71,"title":"[BOUNTY] Ongoing Bug Bounty Program — Find Bugs, Earn RTC (133 RTC Pool)","user":{"login":"Scottcjn","id":121303252,"node_id":"U_kgDOBzrw1A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/121303252?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn","html_url":"https://github.com/Scottcjn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":10115029408,"node_id":"LA_kwDORGgqa88AAAACWucZoA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/labels/bug","name":"bug","color":"d73a4a","default":true,"description":"Something isn't working"},{"id":10115035859,"node_id":"LA_kwDORGgqa88AAAACWucy0w","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/labels/bounty","name":"bounty","color":"0E8A16","default":false,"description":"RTC-paid bounty"},{"id":10115035877,"node_id":"LA_kwDORGgqa88AAAACWucy5Q","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/labels/open","name":"open","color":"1D76DB","default":false,"description":"Open for claims"}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":432,"created_at":"2026-02-06T01:13:53Z","updated_at":"2026-07-07T02:47:44Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"OWNER","active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## Ongoing Bug Bounty Program\n\n**Pool: 750 RTC (ongoing, replenished as needed)**\n\n### Severity & Rewards\n| Severity | Description | Reward |\n|----------|-------------|--------|\n| **Critical** | Fund theft, consensus bypass, RCE | 100-200 RTC |\n| **High** | Data leak, auth bypass, significant logic error | 50-100 RTC |\n| **Medium** | DoS, info disclosure, moderate bugs | 15-50 RTC |\n| **Low** | UI bugs, minor leaks, doc errors | 5-15 RTC |\n\n### In-Scope\n- RustChain node software, attestation & fingerprint system\n- Epoch settlement & rewards, wallet endpoints\n- BoTTube web app, API, payment system\n- Python SDK, Block Explorer, Wallet GUI, Miner clients\n\n### Reporting\n1. Create GitHub issue with `[SECURITY]` prefix\n2. For critical: email first, issue after fix\n3. Include: steps to reproduce, impact, suggested fix\n\n### Rules\n- First reporter wins\n- Responsible disclosure required\n- Must not exploit on production\n\n---\n*Total RTC supply: 8.3M | RTC Reference Rate: 1 RTC = $0.10 USD*","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/71/reactions","total_count":11,"+1":5,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":1,"confused":0,"heart":1,"rocket":3,"eyes":1},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/71/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/Rustchain/issues/165","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/Rustchain","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/Rustchain/issues/165/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/Rustchain/issues/165/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/Rustchain/issues/165/events","html_url":"https://github.com/Scottcjn/Rustchain/issues/165","id":3938981398,"node_id":"I_kwDOOdNtbc7qyBYW","number":165,"title":"[BOUNTY] Share Why You Starred RustChain — 3 RTC + Community Shoutout (Pool: 300 RTC)","user":{"login":"Scottcjn","id":121303252,"node_id":"U_kgDOBzrw1A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/121303252?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn","html_url":"https://github.com/Scottcjn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":8491289527,"node_id":"LA_kwDOOdNtbc8AAAAB-h7Ltw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/Rustchain/labels/help%20wanted","name":"help wanted","color":"008672","default":true,"description":"Extra attention is needed"},{"id":8491289534,"node_id":"LA_kwDOOdNtbc8AAAAB-h7Lvg","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/Rustchain/labels/good%20first%20issue","name":"good first issue","color":"7057FF","default":true,"description":"Good for newcomers (5-10 RTC)"},{"id":10159650136,"node_id":"LA_kwDOOdNtbc8AAAACXY_1WA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/Rustchain/labels/bounty","name":"bounty","color":"0E8A16","default":false,"description":"RTC bounty reward"}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":159,"created_at":"2026-02-13T20:12:59Z","updated_at":"2026-07-07T02:35:55Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"OWNER","active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## Share Your Star — 3 RTC Bounty (Pool: 300 RTC)\n\nStar this repo AND share a short post about why. That's it. Real people sharing real opinions = organic growth.\n\n### How to Claim\n\n1. **Star this repo** (https://github.com/Scottcjn/Rustchain)\n2. **Post about it** on any platform — X/Twitter, Reddit, Mastodon, Dev.to, Hacker News, a blog, Moltbook, anywhere\n3. **Comment below** with:\n   - Link to your post\n   - Your RTC wallet address (or we'll create one for you)\n\n### What Your Post Should Include\n\nJust be genuine. Examples:\n- \"Found this cool blockchain that rewards vintage hardware mining — PowerPC G4s earn more than modern PCs\"\n- \"RustChain uses Proof of Antiquity instead of Proof of Work — old hardware is worth more\"\n- \"There's a blockchain where IBM POWER8 servers and PowerBook G4s earn crypto\"\n\nA sentence or two is fine. No essay needed.\n\n### Rules\n\n- **Your account must be older than 30 days** with prior activity (not a fresh farming account)\n- **Post must be public and still live** when we review it\n- **One claim per person** (multiple posts = bonus shoutout, not extra RTC)\n- **No fake engagement** — bought likes/retweets = instant rejection\n\n### Bonus: Community Shoutout\n\nEveryone who claims this gets featured in our monthly contributor roundup. Best posts get retweeted from [@RustchainPOA](https://x.com/RustchainPOA).\n\n### Payout\n\n3 RTC per valid claim. Pool of 300 RTC = 100 slots available.\n\nFirst come, first served — when the pool's gone, it's gone.\n\n\n---\n\n### ⚖️ Bounty Requirements (FTC 16 CFR §465.5 + §255.5 compliance)\n\n**A star alone does NOT qualify.** We pay for genuine engagement, not for indicators. To claim this bounty you must post a comment (on this issue or a linked post) containing:\n\n1. **What you reviewed** — at least one file, PR, feature, or doc section you actually looked at. Link it.\n2. **Why you liked it** — a specific, non-generic reason. \"Great project\" does not qualify.\n3. **Disclosure** — include the line: `I received RTC compensation for this review.` This keeps your star a transparent endorsement, not a purchased indicator.\n\nStars without a review comment will not be paid. Copy-pasted, AI-templated, or obviously recycled reviews will not be paid. This rule applies retroactively: unreviewed stars from before this update are grandfathered as goodwill but earn no future RTC.\n\n**Why this matters:** Elyan Labs is here to grow real engagement in mining and coding. A star backed by a real review is worth more to the network than a thousand drive-by clicks. This brings us into compliance with the FTC Consumer Review Rule (effective Oct 21, 2024), and — more importantly — keeps the signal honest.\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/Rustchain/issues/165/reactions","total_count":8,"+1":4,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":1,"confused":0,"heart":1,"rocket":1,"eyes":1},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/Rustchain/issues/165/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/455","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/455/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/455/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/455/events","html_url":"https://github.com/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/455","id":4002331192,"node_id":"I_kwDORGgqa87ujro4","number":455,"title":"[25 RTC] Dual-Mining: Ergo (Autolykos2) Integration","user":{"login":"Scottcjn","id":121303252,"node_id":"U_kgDOBzrw1A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/121303252?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn","html_url":"https://github.com/Scottcjn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":10115035859,"node_id":"LA_kwDORGgqa88AAAACWucy0w","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/labels/bounty","name":"bounty","color":"0E8A16","default":false,"description":"RTC-paid bounty"}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":14,"created_at":"2026-02-27T18:34:38Z","updated_at":"2026-07-07T02:35:10Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"OWNER","active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## Ergo Dual-Mining Integration — 25 RTC\n\n**Mine Ergo + earn RTC for free.** RIP-PoA attestation costs zero compute.\n\n### What to Build\n\nImplement and test the Ergo-specific proof path in `clawrtc/data/pow_miners.py`:\n\n1. **Node RPC proof** (1.5x bonus): Query local Ergo node at `localhost:9053/info` — verify `isMining: true`, extract chain height, peer count, best block hash\n2. **Pool account proof** (1.3x bonus): Verify hashrate via HeroMiners, WoolyPooly, Nanopool, or 2miners API\n3. **Server validation**: Add Ergo-specific validation in `validate_pow_proof()` on the RustChain node\n\n### Ergo Node API Reference\n- `GET /info` — node status, mining flag, height\n- `GET /mining/candidate` — current mining candidate (proves active mining)\n- Default port: 9053 (mainnet), 9052 (testnet)\n\n### Testing\n- Run an Ergo node with mining enabled\n- Run `clawrtc mine --pow ergo`\n- Verify proof is generated and accepted by RustChain node\n\n### Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Ergo node auto-detected by port + process\n- [ ] Node RPC proof includes chain height + mining status\n- [ ] Pool verification works for at least 2 pools\n- [ ] Nonce binding prevents proof replay\n- [ ] Unit tests pass\n\nSee master issue: #453","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/455/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":1,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/455/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/458","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/458/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/458/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/458/events","html_url":"https://github.com/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/458","id":4002331744,"node_id":"I_kwDORGgqa87ujrxg","number":458,"title":"[25 RTC] Dual-Mining: Monero (RandomX) Integration","user":{"login":"Scottcjn","id":121303252,"node_id":"U_kgDOBzrw1A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/121303252?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn","html_url":"https://github.com/Scottcjn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":10115035859,"node_id":"LA_kwDORGgqa88AAAACWucy0w","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/labels/bounty","name":"bounty","color":"0E8A16","default":false,"description":"RTC-paid bounty"}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":18,"created_at":"2026-02-27T18:34:43Z","updated_at":"2026-07-07T02:35:10Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"OWNER","active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## Monero Dual-Mining Integration — 25 RTC\n\n**Mine XMR + earn RTC for free.** RandomX is CPU-optimized.\n\n### What to Build\n\n1. **Node RPC proof** (1.5x bonus): Query monerod at `localhost:18081/json_rpc`\n2. **P2Pool proof**: Query local P2Pool at `localhost:18083/local/stats`\n3. **Pool account proof** (1.3x bonus): Verify via HeroMiners or Nanopool\n4. **Process detection**: Detect `xmrig`, `monerod`, `p2pool`, `xmr-stak`\n\n### XMR API Reference\n- `POST /json_rpc` with `{\"method\": \"get_info\"}` — height, difficulty, tx pool\n- Default ports: 18081 (RPC), 18082 (restricted), 18083 (P2Pool)\n\n### Why Monero Miners Love This\nXMRig uses 100% of CPU for RandomX hashing. RIP-PoA runs during attestation windows (5 sec every 10 min) — negligible impact.\n\nSee master issue: #453","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/458/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":1,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/458/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/2161","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/2161/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/2161/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/2161/events","html_url":"https://github.com/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/2161","id":4084034331,"node_id":"I_kwDORGgqa87zbWsb","number":2161,"title":"[BOUNTY: 17 RTC] BoTTube — Creator Collaboration Features","user":{"login":"Scottcjn","id":121303252,"node_id":"U_kgDOBzrw1A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/121303252?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn","html_url":"https://github.com/Scottcjn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":10115035859,"node_id":"LA_kwDORGgqa88AAAACWucy0w","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/labels/bounty","name":"bounty","color":"0E8A16","default":false,"description":"RTC-paid bounty"}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":53,"created_at":"2026-03-16T18:15:15Z","updated_at":"2026-07-07T02:33:02Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"OWNER","active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## Bounty: 25 RTC\n\n### Task\nImplement the feature described in **Scottcjn/bottube#427**.\n\n### How to claim\n1. Read the full spec: https://github.com/Scottcjn/bottube/issues/427\n2. Open a PR on [Scottcjn/bottube](https://github.com/Scottcjn/bottube) implementing the feature\n3. Comment here with your PR link and wallet address\n4. Partial implementations welcome — bounty scales with scope delivered\n\n### Context\nThese features address real user feedback from [ToolPilot.ai reviews](https://www.toolpilot.ai/products/bottube-1) (currently 86% positive, 7 reviews). We're turning 4-star feedback into 5-star features.\n\n**RTC Value: 25 RTC (~$25.00 at $0.10/RTC reference)**","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/2161/reactions","total_count":5,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":1,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":2,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/2161/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/1156","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/1156/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/1156/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/1156/events","html_url":"https://github.com/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/1156","id":4040248415,"node_id":"I_kwDORGgqa87w0Uxf","number":1156,"title":"[BOUNTY: 7-33 RTC] Vintage Hardware Speed Run — Mine RTC on the Weirdest Machine You Own","user":{"login":"Scottcjn","id":121303252,"node_id":"U_kgDOBzrw1A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/121303252?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn","html_url":"https://github.com/Scottcjn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":10115035859,"node_id":"LA_kwDORGgqa88AAAACWucy0w","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/labels/bounty","name":"bounty","color":"0E8A16","default":false,"description":"RTC-paid bounty"}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":30,"created_at":"2026-03-08T02:36:42Z","updated_at":"2026-07-07T02:28:27Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"OWNER","active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## Summary\nRun a real RustChain miner on unusual or vintage hardware and prove that it can successfully attest.\n\n## Why This Matters\nThis bounty is a network-growth and proof-of-antiquity showcase. The point is not just novelty. The point is to demonstrate that real, weird hardware can participate and that the network can verify it cleanly.\n\n## Scope\n- run a RustChain miner on real hardware you own or control\n- use an unusual architecture, vintage system, or otherwise interesting device\n- submit at least one successful attestation\n- preserve enough proof for maintainers to verify the hardware and the mining result\n\n## Reward Tiers\n- `50 RTC` legendary hardware, roughly pre-1995\n- `25 RTC` epic hardware, roughly 1995-2005\n- `15 RTC` unusual architectures or rare boards\n- `10 RTC` uncommon but still interesting x86 or edge devices\n\n## Deliverable\nA verified claim showing a real hardware device mining or attesting on RustChain, with proof that it is not emulated and that the attestation actually landed.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] hardware is real, not emulated or VM-backed\n- [ ] at least one successful attestation is demonstrated\n- [ ] proof includes hardware identity and a real photo of the machine\n- [ ] claim includes the miner ID or attestation reference needed for verification\n- [ ] enough technical detail is included for maintainers to classify the reward tier\n\n## Verification Proof\nPost proof in this issue including:\n- screenshot of the miner running\n- hardware info such as `cpuinfo` or equivalent\n- photo of the physical hardware\n- miner ID or attestation hash\n- your RTC wallet or `miner_id`\n\n## Non-Goals\n- emulators, VMs, or screenshots with no physical-machine proof\n- unverifiable claims with no attestation evidence\n- novelty-only submissions that never actually join the network\n- duplicate claims on the same hardware without meaningful new evidence\n\n## Claim Routing\nUse this issue for hardware proof and payout review. If you hit a real miner bug while bringing unusual hardware online, open a separate issue in `Scottcjn/Rustchain` and link it back here.","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/1156/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/1156/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/bottube/issues/645","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/bottube","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/bottube/issues/645/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/bottube/issues/645/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/bottube/issues/645/events","html_url":"https://github.com/Scottcjn/bottube/issues/645","id":4226223171,"node_id":"I_kwDORFt8-M775wxD","number":645,"title":"[BOUNTY: 15 RTC] Record LLM Inference on Unusual Hardware","user":{"login":"sophiaeagent-beep","id":245112282,"node_id":"U_kgDODpwd2g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/245112282?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sophiaeagent-beep","html_url":"https://github.com/sophiaeagent-beep","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sophiaeagent-beep/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sophiaeagent-beep/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sophiaeagent-beep/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sophiaeagent-beep/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sophiaeagent-beep/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sophiaeagent-beep/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sophiaeagent-beep/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sophiaeagent-beep/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sophiaeagent-beep/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":10119976340,"node_id":"LA_kwDORFt8-M8AAAACWzKVlA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/bottube/labels/bounty","name":"bounty","color":"BFDADC","default":false,"description":""}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":8,"created_at":"2026-04-08T17:02:11Z","updated_at":"2026-07-07T02:14:57Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"OWNER","active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## Bounty: 15 RTC\n\n### The Challenge\nRecord a video of an LLM running on unusual/vintage/exotic hardware and upload to BoTTube.\n\n### Examples That Qualify\n- llama.cpp on a Raspberry Pi\n- LLM on POWER8 (see [llama-cpp-power8](https://github.com/Scottcjn/llama-cpp-power8))\n- ChatBot on a PowerPC Mac\n- Inference on a phone, tablet, or game console\n- Any hardware that makes people say \"wait, that runs an LLM?\"\n\n### Requirements\n- Video shows the LLM generating text on the hardware\n- Show the hardware itself (a photo or camera shot)\n- Upload to BoTTube with tags `#LLM` `#inference`\n- Post link here\n\n### Bonus\n- +10 RTC if hardware is PPA-verified (run fingerprint_checks.py too)\n- +5 RTC if you use [llama-cpp-power8](https://github.com/Scottcjn/llama-cpp-power8) optimizations\n\n*Posted by @sophiaeagent-beep — Sophia Elya, Elyan Labs*","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/bottube/issues/645/reactions","total_count":6,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":1,"confused":0,"heart":1,"rocket":1,"eyes":1},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/bottube/issues/645/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/2781","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/2781/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/2781/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/2781/events","html_url":"https://github.com/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/2781","id":4195434807,"node_id":"I_kwDORGgqa876EUE3","number":2781,"title":"[ONBOARD: 1 RTC] File Your First Bug Report","user":{"login":"Scottcjn","id":121303252,"node_id":"U_kgDOBzrw1A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/121303252?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn","html_url":"https://github.com/Scottcjn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":10115029430,"node_id":"LA_kwDORGgqa88AAAACWucZtg","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/labels/good%20first%20issue","name":"good first issue","color":"7057ff","default":true,"description":"Good for newcomers"},{"id":10115035859,"node_id":"LA_kwDORGgqa88AAAACWucy0w","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/labels/bounty","name":"bounty","color":"0E8A16","default":false,"description":"RTC-paid bounty"},{"id":10360962887,"node_id":"LA_kwDORGgqa88AAAACaY-_Rw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/labels/onboarding","name":"onboarding","color":"ededed","default":false,"description":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":237,"created_at":"2026-04-02T15:41:22Z","updated_at":"2026-07-07T02:07:51Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"OWNER","active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## Bounty: 1 RTC\n\n### What You'll Do\nGet familiar with RustChain by exploring the codebase and reporting something real.\n\n### Steps\n1. **Explore** the README, docs, or try running the miner in `--dry-run` mode\n2. **File a bug report** on [Rustchain issues](https://github.com/Scottcjn/Rustchain/issues). This can be:\n   - A broken link you found\n   - A confusing error message\n   - A doc section that confused you as a newcomer\n   - An actual bug\n3. **Comment here** with a link to your issue\n\n### What Counts\n- The issue must be **real and specific** (not \"the docs could be better\")\n- Duplicate issues don't count, check existing issues first\n- Your fresh-eyes perspective is genuinely valuable. Newcomers find things veterans miss.\n\n### Payment\n1 RTC once your issue is verified as a real finding.\n\n### Why This Exists\nEvery open-source project needs fresh eyes. Your first contribution starts with looking at the code and telling us what's broken or confusing.\n\n**Difficulty**: Easy | **Time**: 15-30 min | **Skills**: Reading comprehension\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/2781/reactions","total_count":10,"+1":5,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":1,"confused":0,"heart":1,"rocket":2,"eyes":1},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/2781/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/editorconfig/editorconfig/issues/228","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/editorconfig/editorconfig","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/editorconfig/editorconfig/issues/228/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/editorconfig/editorconfig/issues/228/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/editorconfig/editorconfig/issues/228/events","html_url":"https://github.com/editorconfig/editorconfig/issues/228","id":98364903,"node_id":"MDU6SXNzdWU5ODM2NDkwMw==","number":228,"title":"Add property for files that should be not listed or not indexed for search","user":{"login":"adelgado","id":762070,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2MjA3MA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/762070?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/adelgado","html_url":"https://github.com/adelgado","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adelgado/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adelgado/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adelgado/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adelgado/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adelgado/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adelgado/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adelgado/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adelgado/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adelgado/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":1948429,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxOTQ4NDI5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/editorconfig/editorconfig/labels/feature%20request","name":"feature request","color":"02e10c","default":false,"description":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":58,"created_at":"2015-07-31T10:43:24Z","updated_at":"2026-07-07T02:02:06Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"First of all, I did a search on the issues but couldn't find a similar proposal, so here it goes:\n\nIt'd be nice to have a property holding a list of files or file-globs that either (1) should not be displayed on some file listing (e.g. a folder tree pane), or (2) should not be indexed and/or displayed as search results between a repository.\n\nBasically analogous to Sublime's `file_exclude_patterns`, `folder_exclude_patterns` and `index_exclude_patterns`.\n\nA real-life use case is that I don't want compilation artifacts to be indexed for search, and I'd like to be able to configure that explicitly per-repository.\n\nHow do you feel about it?\n\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/editorconfig/editorconfig/issues/228/reactions","total_count":97,"+1":86,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":11,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/editorconfig/editorconfig/issues/228/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/peleduri/zero-day-pulse/issues/7","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/peleduri/zero-day-pulse","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/peleduri/zero-day-pulse/issues/7/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/peleduri/zero-day-pulse/issues/7/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/peleduri/zero-day-pulse/issues/7/events","html_url":"https://github.com/peleduri/zero-day-pulse/issues/7","id":4525015280,"node_id":"I_kwDOSkrEes8AAAABDbZA8A","number":7,"title":"🚨 Zero Day Pulse — Active Vulnerability Tracker","user":{"login":"github-actions[bot]","id":41898282,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/15368?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/github-actions","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":11025306354,"node_id":"LA_kwDOSkrEes8AAAACkSjS8g","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/peleduri/zero-day-pulse/labels/zero-day-pulse","name":"zero-day-pulse","color":"ededed","default":false,"description":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":168,"created_at":"2026-05-26T14:37:26Z","updated_at":"2026-07-07T02:00:46Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"# Zero Day Pulse\n\n> **Generated:** 2026-05-26 14:37 UTC &nbsp;|&nbsp; **Total:** 15 &nbsp;|&nbsp; 🔴 KEV: 0 &nbsp;|&nbsp; 🟠 Zero-Day: 13 &nbsp;|&nbsp; 🟡 High: 2 &nbsp;|&nbsp; ✨ Enriched: 10\n\n---\n\n## 1. 🟠 Zero-Day — Ransomware Actors Exploit Unpatched SimpleHelp Remote Monitoring and Management to Compromise Utility Billing Software Provider\n\n**CVE:** `CVE-2024-57727` &nbsp;|&nbsp; **Source:** CISA US-CERT Alerts &nbsp;|&nbsp; **Published:** Thu, 12 Ju\n**Reference:** <https://www.cisa.gov/news-events/cybersecurity-advisories/aa25-163a>\n\n> Summary The Cybersecurity and Infrastructure Security Agency (CISA) is releasing this advisory in response to ransomware actors leveraging unpatched instances of a vulnerability in SimpleHelp Remote Monitoring and Management (RMM) to compromise customers of a utility billing software provider. This incident reflects a broader pattern of ransomware actors targeting organizations through unpatched v…\n\n**Parallel AI Enrichment:**\n\n- **Technical Details:** CVE-2024-57727 is a path traversal vulnerability in SimpleHelp (v5.5.7 and earlier) enabling unauthenticated attackers to retrieve logs, configuration files, credentials and potentially gain access to downstream systems.\n- **Affected Products:** SimpleHelp remote support software v5.5.7 and earlier\n- **CVSS Score:** 7.5\n- **CVSS Vector:** CVSS vector unavailable\n- **Exploit Available:** true (https://medium.com/@RosanaFS/simplehelp-cve-2024-57727-tryhackme-walkthrough-9f88c2061fb9)\n- **Patch Available:** true (http://community.simple-help.com/t/simplehelp-5-5-8-critical-security-fixes/1570)\n- **Active Exploitation:** true (https://www.cisa.gov/news-events/cybersecurity-advisories/aa25-163a)\n- **Threat Actors:** Ransomware actors (e.g., DragonForce)\n- **Mitigation:** Apply vendor patch to v5.5.8 immediately; if unable, isolate SimpleHelp RMM from internet, restrict access to management interfaces, apply network segmentation, rotate exposed credentials, enable logging and monitoring, and follow CISA incident response guidance.\n- **Vendor Advisory:** http://simple-help.com/blogs/security-vulnerabilities-in-simplehelp-5-5-7-and-earlier-what-you-need-to-know\n\n---\n\n## 2. 🟠 Zero-Day — Hackers Exploited KnowledgeDeliver Zero-Day for Web Shell Deployment\n\n**CVE:** _No CVE_ &nbsp;|&nbsp; **Source:** SecurityWeek &nbsp;|&nbsp; **Published:** 2026-05-26\n**Reference:** <https://www.securityweek.com/hackers-exploited-knowledgedeliver-zero-day-for-web-shell-deployment/>\n\n> Hardcoded machineKey values in a configuration file enabled ViewState deserialization attacks leading to remote code execution. The post Hackers Exploited KnowledgeDeliver Zero-Day for Web Shell Deployment appeared first on SecurityWeek .\n\n**Parallel AI Enrichment:**\n\n- **Technical Details:** Hard‑coded ASP.NET machineKey values enable attackers who obtain the key to create malicious __VIEWSTATE payloads that bypass validation, causing deserialization and unauthenticated remote code execution; the breach culminates in deployment of in‑memory BLUEBEAM (Godzilla) web shells.\n- **Affected Products:** Digital Knowledge KnowledgeDeliver (installations deployed before Feb 24, 2026)\n- **CVSS Score:** 7.5\n- **CVSS Vector:** CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:N/A:N\n- **Exploit Available:** true\n- **Patch Available:** true\n- **Active Exploitation:** true\n- **Threat Actors:** Unknown specific group; Mandiant reports an \"unknown threat actor\"\n- **Mitigation:** Immediately rotate machineKey to unique cryptographically strong values per instance; restrict external access (IP allowlist); monitor Event ID 1316 and ViewState integrity failures, and hunt for suspicious w3wp.exe child processes and related IOCs.\n- **Vendor Advisory:** Vendor advisory URL unavailable.\n\n---\n\n## 3. 🟠 Zero-Day — Iranian Hackers Deploy MiniFast and MiniJunk V2 via Phishing and SEO Poisoning\n\n**CVE:** _No CVE_ &nbsp;|&nbsp; **Source:** The Hacker News Security &nbsp;|&nbsp; **Published:** 2026-05-26\n**Reference:** <https://thehackernews.com/2026/05/iranian-hackers-deploy-minifast-and.html>\n\n> The Iranian state-sponsored threat actor known as Nimbus Manticore (aka Screening Serpens and UNC1549) has been attributed to a fresh campaign using lures impersonating organizations in the aviation and software sectors across the U.S., Europe, and the Middle East following the joint U.S.-Israeli military campaign against the country in late February 2026.\n\nThe activity, besides embracing\n\n**Parallel AI Enrichment:**\n\n- **Technical Details:** Campaigns use SEO poisoning and spear/phishing lures to deliver MiniFast (AI‑assisted) and MiniJunk V2 implants. Delivery vectors include malicious links and attachments; implants perform espionage (recon, credential harvesting, persistence) and likely leverage cloud services (reported abuse of Microsoft Azure) for hosting C2 and payloads.\n- **Affected Products:** Affected products unavailable.\n- **CVSS Score:** CVSS score unavailable.\n- **CVSS Vector:** CVSS vector unavailable.\n- **Exploit Available:** false\n- **Patch Available:** false\n- **Active Exploitation:** true\n- **Threat Actors:** Nimbus Manticore (aka Screening Serpens, UNC1549)\n- **Mitigation:** Increase email security and phishing awareness; block known malicious domains and SEO‑poisoned landing pages; implement URL filtering and web proxying; enable EDR/anti‑malware with YARA/signature and behavior detections; disable/limit macros and script execution; apply least‑privilege and multi‑factor authentication; isolate and investigate suspected hosts.\n- **Vendor Advisory:** Vendor advisory URL unavailable.\n\n---\n\n## 4. 🟠 Zero-Day — AI threats in the wild: The current state of prompt injections on the web\n\n**CVE:** _No CVE_ &nbsp;|&nbsp; **Source:** Google Security Blog &nbsp;|&nbsp; **Published:** 2026-04-23\n**Reference:** <http://security.googleblog.com/2026/04/ai-threats-in-wild-current-state-of.html>\n\n> Posted by Thomas Brunner, Yu-Han Liu, Moni Pande At Google, our Threat Intelligence teams are dedicated to staying ahead of real-world adversarial activity, proactively monitoring emerging threats before they can impact users. Right now, Indirect Prompt Injection (IPI) is a top priority for the security community, anticipating it as a primary attack vector for adversaries to target and compromise …\n\n**Parallel AI Enrichment:**\n\n- **Technical Details:** Indirect Prompt Injection (IPI) occurs when adversarial content hosted on public web pages or other untrusted sources contains instructions or payloads that an LLM‑powered agent ingests as part of its context, causing it to execute unintended actions (data exfiltration, API key theft, command execution via agent frameworks). Attack vectors include crafted web pages, embedded comments, README files, or other content that agents fetch when following web browsing or tool‑use capabilities.\n- **Affected Products:** Affected products unavailable\n- **CVSS Score:** CVSS score unavailable.\n- **CVSS Vector:** CVSS vector unavailable.\n- **Exploit Available:** true — https://www.forcepoint.com/blog/x-labs/indirect-prompt-injection-payloads\n- **Patch Available:** false — https://microsoft.com/en-us/security/blog/2026/05/07/prompts-become-shells-rce-vulnerabilities-ai-agent-frameworks\n- **Active Exploitation:** true — Sources: https://www.forcepoint.com/blog/x-labs/indirect-prompt-injection-payloads, http://security.googleblog.com/2026/04/ai-threats-in-wild-current-state-of.html\n- **Threat Actors:** None known\n- **Mitigation:** Implement input provenance controls, remote content filtering, strict instruction parsing, principle of least privilege for agents, sanitize and ignore untrusted web-origin instructions, use model grounding and instruction allowlists/denylists, robust content security policies.\n- **Vendor Advisory:** http://security.googleblog.com/2026/04/ai-threats-in-wild-current-state-of.html\n\n---\n\n## 5. 🟠 Zero-Day — Google Workspace’s continuous approach to mitigating indirect prompt injections\n\n**CVE:** _No CVE_ &nbsp;|&nbsp; **Source:** Google Security Blog &nbsp;|&nbsp; **Published:** 2026-04-02\n**Reference:** <http://security.googleblog.com/2026/04/google-workspaces-continuous-approach.html>\n\n> Posted by Adam Gavish, Google GenAI Security Team Indirect prompt injection (IPI) is an evolving threat vector targeting users of complex AI applications with multiple data sources, such as Workspace with Gemini. This technique enables the attacker to influence the behavior of an LLM by injecting malicious instructions into the data or tools used by the LLM as it completes the user’s query. This m…\n\n**Parallel AI Enrichment:**\n\n- **Technical Details:** Indirect prompt injection (IPI) exploits the ability of large language models to consume data from multiple sources. By inserting crafted malicious instructions into those sources or associated tools, an attacker can steer the model’s output or actions even when the user does not directly provide malicious input.\n- **Affected Products:** Google Workspace (Gemini), Gemini CLI\n- **CVSS Score:** 10.0\n- **CVSS Vector:** CVSS vector unavailable.\n- **Exploit Available:** Exploit availability unknown.\n- **Patch Available:** true\n- **Active Exploitation:** true\n- **Threat Actors:** Threat actors unknown.\n- **Mitigation:** Apply the latest Google Workspace and Gemini CLI patches, enable Google’s continuous mitigation controls, monitor logs for anomalous prompt activity, and restrict the use of automated agents that can ingest untrusted data.\n- **Vendor Advisory:** http://security.googleblog.com/2026/04/google-workspaces-continuous-approach.html\n\n---\n\n## 6. 🟠 Zero-Day — Architecting Security for Agentic Capabilities in Chrome\n\n**CVE:** _No CVE_ &nbsp;|&nbsp; **Source:** Google Security Blog &nbsp;|&nbsp; **Published:** 2025-12-08\n**Reference:** <http://security.googleblog.com/2025/12/architecting-security-for-agentic.html>\n\n> Posted by Nathan Parker, Chrome security team Chrome has been advancing the web’s security for well over 15 years, and we’re committed to meeting new challenges and opportunities with AI. Billions of people trust Chrome to keep them safe by default, and this is a responsibility we take seriously. Following the recent launch of Gemini in Chrome and the preview of agentic capabilities , we want to s…\n\n**Parallel AI Enrichment:**\n\n- **Technical Details:** Chrome's agentic features face \"indirect prompt injection\": malicious instructions embedded in web content (pages, iframes, UGC) can influence an agent to perform unwanted actions (e.g., transactions, exfiltration). Google describes layered defenses: origin gating, a User Alignment Critic classifier, planner/gating function separation, explicit user confirmations for sensitive actions, Safe Browsing and on‑device scam detection, and work‑logs for transparency.\n- **Affected Products:** Affected products unavailable.\n- **CVSS Score:** CVSS score unavailable.\n- **CVSS Vector:** CVSS vector unavailable.\n- **Exploit Available:** false.\n- **Patch Available:** true; https://blog.google/security/architecting-security-for-agentic/\n- **Active Exploitation:** false.\n- **Threat Actors:** None known.\n- **Mitigation:** Use Google’s layered defenses and hardening: enable the latest Chrome updates with agentic protections; rely on origin gating and user confirmations; monitor Safe Browsing and on‑device protections; follow Google guidance in the vendor advisory; consider blocking agentic browsers in high‑risk environments per Gartner/NCSC guidance.\n- **Vendor Advisory:** https://blog.google/security/architecting-security-for-agentic/\n\n---\n\n## 7. 🟠 Zero-Day — Rust in Android: move fast and fix things\n\n**CVE:** _No CVE_ &nbsp;|&nbsp; **Source:** Google Security Blog &nbsp;|&nbsp; **Published:** 2025-11-13\n**Reference:** <http://security.googleblog.com/2025/11/rust-in-android-move-fast-fix-things.html>\n\n> Posted by Jeff Vander Stoep, Android Last year, we wrote about why a memory safety strategy that focuses on vulnerability prevention in new code quickly yields durable and compounding gains. This year we look at how this approach isn’t just fixing things, but helping us move faster . The 2025 data continues to validate the approach, with memory safety vulnerabilities falling below 20% of total vul…\n\n**Parallel AI Enrichment:**\n\n- **Technical Details:** Google reports that adopting Rust in Android reduced memory‑safety vulnerability density (2025 data shows memory safety vulnerabilities fell below 20% of total vulnerabilities), reflecting a prevention‑first strategy focused on new code; Rust prevents classes of memory‑safety bugs common in C/C++.\n- **Affected Products:** Affected products unavailable.\n- **CVSS Score:** CVSS score unavailable.\n- **CVSS Vector:** CVSS vector unavailable.\n- **Exploit Available:** Exploit availability unknown.\n- **Patch Available:** Patch availability unknown.\n- **Active Exploitation:** Active exploitation status unknown.\n- **Threat Actors:** None known\n- **Mitigation:** Use memory‑safe languages (Rust) for new code, prioritize vulnerability prevention in code changes, continue auditing C/C++ components and apply defensive coding and sanitizers.\n- **Vendor Advisory:** http://security.googleblog.com/2025/11/rust-in-android-move-fast-fix-things.html\n\n---\n\n## 8. 🟠 Zero-Day — Mitigating prompt injection attacks with a layered defense strategy\n\n**CVE:** _No CVE_ &nbsp;|&nbsp; **Source:** Google Security Blog &nbsp;|&nbsp; **Published:** 2025-06-13\n**Reference:** <http://security.googleblog.com/2025/06/mitigating-prompt-injection-attacks.html>\n\n> Posted by Adam Gavish, Google GenAI Security Team With the rapid adoption of generative AI, a new wave of threats is emerging across the industry with the aim of manipulating the AI systems themselves. One such emerging attack vector is indirect prompt injections. Unlike direct prompt injections, where an attacker directly inputs malicious commands into a prompt, indirect prompt injections involve…\n\n**Parallel AI Enrichment:**\n\n- **Technical Details:** Indirect prompt injection (IPI) is an attack where hidden or external instructions (e.g., in emails, documents, calendar invites, or web content) are crafted to manipulate generative AI systems that ingest external data, causing them to disclose sensitive information or perform unauthorized actions. The mechanism relies on models browsing or ingesting untrusted external content which contains adversarial instructions that the model treats as part of its prompt.\n- **Affected Products:** Affected products unavailable\n- **CVSS Score:** CVSS score unavailable\n- **CVSS Vector:** CVSS vector unavailable\n- **Exploit Available:** false\n- **Patch Available:** false\n- **Active Exploitation:** true\n- **Threat Actors:** None known\n- **Mitigation:** Apply a layered defense strategy including input provenance and validation (treat external data as untrusted), content filtering and sanitization, model instruction hardening (instruction‑following constraints and refusal policies), strict data access controls and least‑privilege for model actions, rate‑limiting and monitoring for anomalous queries, and use of browser/browsing isolation when allowing models to access web content.\n- **Vendor Advisory:** http://security.googleblog.com/2025/06/mitigating-prompt-injection-attacks.html\n\n---\n\n## 9. 🟠 Zero-Day — Countering Chinese State-Sponsored Actors Compromise of Networks Worldwide to Feed Global Espionage System\n\n**CVE:** _No CVE_ &nbsp;|&nbsp; **Source:** CISA US-CERT Alerts &nbsp;|&nbsp; **Published:** Mon, 25 Au\n**Reference:** <https://www.cisa.gov/news-events/cybersecurity-advisories/aa25-239a>\n\n> Executive summary People’s Republic of China (PRC) state-sponsored cyber threat actors are targeting networks globally, including, but not limited to, telecommunications, government, transportation, lodging, and military infrastructure networks. While these actors focus on large backbone routers of major telecommunications providers, as well as provider edge (PE) and customer edge (CE) routers, th…\n\n**Parallel AI Enrichment:**\n\n- **Technical Details:** Actors modify routers to maintain persistent, long‑term access and leverage compromised devices and trusted connections to pivot into other networks.\n- **Affected Products:** Backbone routers, Provider Edge (PE) routers, Customer Edge (CE) routers\n- **CVSS Score:** CVSS score unavailable.\n- **CVSS Vector:** CVSS vector unavailable.\n- **Exploit Available:** Exploit availability unknown.\n- **Patch Available:** Patch availability unknown.\n- **Active Exploitation:** Active exploitation status unknown.\n- **Threat Actors:** Salt Typhoon, OPERATOR PANDA, RedMike, UNC5807, GhostEmperor\n- **Mitigation:** Follow CISA’s mitigation guidance: simulate the threat scenarios, apply router hardening best practices, enforce network segmentation, and regularly update firmware.\n- **Vendor Advisory:** https://www.cisa.gov/news-events/cybersecurity-advisories/aa25-239a\n\n---\n\n## 10. 🟠 Zero-Day — Russian GRU Targeting Western Logistics Entities and Technology Companies\n\n**CVE:** _No CVE_ &nbsp;|&nbsp; **Source:** CISA US-CERT Alerts &nbsp;|&nbsp; **Published:** Mon, 12 Ma\n**Reference:** <https://www.cisa.gov/news-events/cybersecurity-advisories/aa25-141a>\n\n> Executive Summary This joint cybersecurity advisory (CSA) highlights a Russian state-sponsored cyber campaign targeting Western logistics entities and technology companies. This includes those involved in the coordination, transport, and delivery of foreign assistance to Ukraine. Since 2022, Western logistics entities and IT companies have faced an elevated risk of targeting by the Russian General…\n\n**Parallel AI Enrichment:**\n\n- **Technical Details:** Technical details unavailable\n- **Affected Products:** Affected products unavailable\n- **CVSS Score:** CVSS score unavailable\n- **CVSS Vector:** CVSS vector unavailable\n- **Exploit Available:** Exploit availability unknown\n- **Patch Available:** Patch availability unknown\n- **Active Exploitation:** true\n- **Threat Actors:** Russian General Staff Main Intelligence Directorate (GRU) 85th Main Special Service Center (85th GTsSS), military unit 26165 (aka APT28)\n- **Mitigation:** Follow advisory hardening and detection recommendations (network segmentation, multifactor authentication, patching where applicable, enhanced monitoring/logging, restrict remote access, incident response planning). See vendor advisory for full mitigations.\n- **Vendor Advisory:** https://www.cisa.gov/news-events/cybersecurity-advisories/aa25-141a\n\n---\n\n## 11. 🟠 Zero-Day — CISA orders feds to patch actively exploited Drupal vulnerability\n\n**CVE:** _No CVE_ &nbsp;|&nbsp; **Source:** Bleeping Computer &nbsp;|&nbsp; **Published:** 2026-05-26\n**Reference:** <https://www.bleepingcomputer.com/news/security/cisa-orders-feds-to-patch-actively-exploited-drupal-vulnerability/>\n\n> CISA has given U.S. government agencies until Wednesday evening to secure their servers against an SQL injection vulnerability in the Drupal content management system (CMS) that it flagged as actively exploited. [...]\n\n---\n\n## 12. 🟠 Zero-Day — KnowledgeDeliver LMS Flaw Exploited to Deploy Godzilla and Cobalt Strike\n\n**CVE:** `CVE-2026-5426` &nbsp;|&nbsp; **Source:** The Hacker News Security &nbsp;|&nbsp; **Published:** 2026-05-26\n**Reference:** <https://thehackernews.com/2026/05/knowledgedeliver-lms-flaw-exploited-to.html>\n\n> A now-patched high-severity security flaw affecting Digital Knowledge KnowledgeDeliver, a Learning Management System (LMS) popular in Japan, was exploited as a zero-day to deliver the Godzilla web shell and ultimately facilitate the deployment of Cobalt Strike Beacon.\n\nThe vulnerability, tracked as CVE-2026-5426 (CVSS score: 7.5), stems from the use of hard-coded ASP.NET machine keys, leading to\n\n---\n\n## 13. 🟠 Zero-Day — [SECURITY ADVISORY] CVE-2026-34474 - ZTE H298A/H108N Unauthenticated Admin Credential Exposure\n\n**CVE:** `CVE-2026-34474` &nbsp;|&nbsp; **Source:** Full Disclosure &nbsp;|&nbsp; **Published:** 2026-05-26\n**Reference:** <https://seclists.org/fulldisclosure/2026/May/20>\n\n> Posted by m.nageh on May 25 -----BEGIN SECURITY ADVISORY----- Advisory ID: MONX-2026-003 CVE ID: CVE-2026-34474 Title: ZTE ZXHN H298A / H108N - Unauthenticated Admin Password &amp; WLAN Credential Exposure Affected: ZTE ZXHN H298A 1.1, ZTE ZXHN H108N 2.6 (EOL; no patch planned) Date: 2026-05-20 Author: Mina Nageh Salalma (Monx Research) Contact: minanageh379 () gmail com Public URL:...\n\n---\n\n## 14. 🟡 High Severity — Microsoft Patches SharePoint RCE Flaw CVE-2026-45659 Across Server Versions\n\n**CVE:** `CVE-2026-45659` &nbsp;|&nbsp; **Source:** The Hacker News Security &nbsp;|&nbsp; **Published:** 2026-05-26\n**Reference:** <https://thehackernews.com/2026/05/microsoft-patches-sharepoint-rce-flaw.html>\n\n> Microsoft has rolled out updates to fix a remote code execution vulnerability impacting SharePoint that could be exploited by bad actors in attacks without requiring any specialized conditions to be met.\n\nThe vulnerability, tracked as CVE-2026-45659, carries a CVSS score of 8.8. It has been assigned an important severity.\n\n&quot;Deserialization of untrusted data in Microsoft Office SharePoint allo…\n\n---\n\n## 15. 🟡 High Severity — Bringing Rust to the Pixel Baseband\n\n**CVE:** `CVE-2024-27227` &nbsp;|&nbsp; **Source:** Google Security Blog &nbsp;|&nbsp; **Published:** 2026-04-10\n**Reference:** <http://security.googleblog.com/2026/04/bringing-rust-to-pixel-baseband.html>\n\n> Posted by Jiacheng Lu, Software Engineer, Google Pixel Team Google is continuously advancing the security of Pixel devices. We have been focusing on hardening the cellular baseband modem against exploitation. Recognizing the risks associated within the complex modem firmware, Pixel 9 shipped with mitigations against a range of memory-safety vulnerabilities. For Pixel 10, Google is advancing its pr…\n\n---\n\n\n---\n[Live dashboard](https://peleduri.github.io/zero-day-pulse/) · [Raw JSON](https://github.com/peleduri/zero-day-pulse/blob/main/reports/latest.json) · [Action run](https://github.com/peleduri/zero-day-pulse/actions/runs/26454818922)","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/peleduri/zero-day-pulse/issues/7/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/peleduri/zero-day-pulse/issues/7/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/Rustchain/issues/773","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/Rustchain","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/Rustchain/issues/773/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/Rustchain/issues/773/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/Rustchain/issues/773/events","html_url":"https://github.com/Scottcjn/Rustchain/issues/773","id":4047382745,"node_id":"I_kwDOOdNtbc7xPijZ","number":773,"title":"[BOUNTY] Star the repo and share why (0.5 RTC)","user":{"login":"Scottcjn","id":121303252,"node_id":"U_kgDOBzrw1A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/121303252?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn","html_url":"https://github.com/Scottcjn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":8491289534,"node_id":"LA_kwDOOdNtbc8AAAAB-h7Lvg","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/Rustchain/labels/good%20first%20issue","name":"good first issue","color":"7057FF","default":true,"description":"Good for newcomers (5-10 RTC)"},{"id":10159650136,"node_id":"LA_kwDOOdNtbc8AAAACXY_1WA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/Rustchain/labels/bounty","name":"bounty","color":"0E8A16","default":false,"description":"RTC bounty reward"},{"id":10211346383,"node_id":"LA_kwDOOdNtbc8AAAACYKTHzw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/Rustchain/labels/community","name":"community","color":"ededed","default":false,"description":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":145,"created_at":"2026-03-09T19:09:20Z","updated_at":"2026-07-07T01:52:42Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"OWNER","active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## Bounty: 0.5 RTC\n\nStar the RustChain repo and leave a comment on this issue explaining what interested you about the project.\n\n### Rules\n- Must actually star the repo (we verify)\n- Comment must be genuine (2+ sentences, not copy-paste)\n- One claim per GitHub account\n- Include your wallet ID in your comment\n\n### How to claim\n1. Star this repo ⭐\n2. Comment below with what caught your eye + your wallet ID\n3. We'll send 0.5 RTC within 48 hours\n\n**Pool: 25 RTC** (50 stars)\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n\n---\n\n### ⚖️ Bounty Requirements (FTC 16 CFR §465.5 + §255.5 compliance)\n\n**A star alone does NOT qualify.** We pay for genuine engagement, not for indicators. To claim this bounty you must post a comment (on this issue or a linked post) containing:\n\n1. **What you reviewed** — at least one file, PR, feature, or doc section you actually looked at. Link it.\n2. **Why you liked it** — a specific, non-generic reason. \"Great project\" does not qualify.\n3. **Disclosure** — include the line: `I received RTC compensation for this review.` This keeps your star a transparent endorsement, not a purchased indicator.\n\nStars without a review comment will not be paid. Copy-pasted, AI-templated, or obviously recycled reviews will not be paid. This rule applies retroactively: unreviewed stars from before this update are grandfathered as goodwill but earn no future RTC.\n\n**Why this matters:** Elyan Labs is here to grow real engagement in mining and coding. A star backed by a real review is worth more to the network than a thousand drive-by clicks. This brings us into compliance with the FTC Consumer Review Rule (effective Oct 21, 2024), and — more importantly — keeps the signal honest.\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/Rustchain/issues/773/reactions","total_count":11,"+1":4,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":2,"confused":0,"heart":3,"rocket":1,"eyes":1},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/Rustchain/issues/773/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/2819","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/2819/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/2819/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/2819/events","html_url":"https://github.com/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/2819","id":4203177266,"node_id":"I_kwDORGgqa876h2Uy","number":2819,"title":"[BOUNTY] Red Team UTXO Implementation — Find Bugs, Earn RTC (33-133 RTC)","user":{"login":"Scottcjn","id":121303252,"node_id":"U_kgDOBzrw1A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/121303252?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn","html_url":"https://github.com/Scottcjn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":10115029422,"node_id":"LA_kwDORGgqa88AAAACWucZrg","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/labels/help%20wanted","name":"help wanted","color":"008672","default":true,"description":"Extra attention is needed"},{"id":10115035859,"node_id":"LA_kwDORGgqa88AAAACWucy0w","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/labels/bounty","name":"bounty","color":"0E8A16","default":false,"description":"RTC-paid bounty"},{"id":10334947395,"node_id":"LA_kwDORGgqa88AAAACaALIQw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/labels/security","name":"security","color":"ededed","default":false,"description":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":176,"created_at":"2026-04-04T03:03:17Z","updated_at":"2026-07-07T01:44:51Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"OWNER","active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## Overview\n\nRustChain is migrating from an account-based balance model to a full UTXO (Unspent Transaction Output) model. **Phase 1+2 just landed** in [`39bf02b`](https://github.com/Scottcjn/Rustchain/commit/39bf02b).\n\nWe want adversarial eyes on this before enabling dual-write on production. Break it, get paid.\n\n## Files to Review\n\nAll in the [`node/`](https://github.com/Scottcjn/Rustchain/tree/main/node) directory of the main Rustchain repo:\n\n| File | Lines | Purpose |\n|------|-------|---------|\n| `utxo_db.py` | ~708 | Core UTXO database layer — UTXOs, transactions, mempool, Merkle roots, coin selection |\n| `test_utxo_db.py` | ~421 | 29 unit tests covering the UTXO layer |\n| `utxo_genesis_migration.py` | ~272 | Deterministic migration of 538 existing account balances into genesis UTXOs |\n| `rustchain_v2_integrated_v2.2.1_rip200.py` | (diff) | Server integration — imports + table init behind `UTXO_DUAL_WRITE` feature flag |\n\n## What to Look For\n\n### Critical Vectors (200 RTC)\n- **Double-spend attacks** — Can the same UTXO be consumed twice? Race conditions in `apply_transaction()`?\n- **Fund creation from nothing** — Can a transaction create more RTC in outputs than exists in inputs?\n- **Genesis migration tampering** — Can the migration be re-run to duplicate balances?\n\n### High Severity (100 RTC)\n- **Race conditions** — Concurrent transaction application, TOCTOU between validation and commitment\n- **Conservation law bypass** — Any path where `sum(inputs) != sum(outputs) + fee`\n- **Lock/unlock logic errors** — Can locked UTXOs be spent? Can spending bypass the lock check?\n\n### Medium Severity (50 RTC)\n- **Mempool DoS** — Can the mempool be flooded or manipulated to block legitimate transactions?\n- **Merkle state root manipulation** — Can the state root be made to diverge between nodes?\n- **Fee calculation exploits** — Negative fees, integer overflow in fee math, fee-free transactions that should require fees\n\n### Low Severity (25 RTC)\n- **Coin selection edge cases** — Pathological wallet states that break coin selection\n- **Code quality issues** — SQL injection vectors, unchecked error paths, missing validations\n- **Test coverage gaps** — Important scenarios not covered by the 29 existing tests\n\n## How to Submit\n\n**Option A (preferred):** Open a PR on [Scottcjn/Rustchain](https://github.com/Scottcjn/Rustchain) with a **failing test case** that demonstrates the bug. Title it `[UTXO-BUG] <description>`.\n\n**Option B:** Open an issue on this repo with a detailed writeup including:\n1. The vulnerability class\n2. Steps to reproduce\n3. Expected vs actual behavior\n4. Suggested fix (optional but earns bonus)\n\n## Bounty Tiers Summary\n\n| Severity | Payout | Examples |\n|----------|--------|----------|\n| **Critical** | **200 RTC** | Double-spend, fund creation, genesis duplication |\n| **High** | **100 RTC** | Race conditions, conservation bypass |\n| **Medium** | **50 RTC** | Mempool DoS, Merkle manipulation |\n| **Low** | **25 RTC** | Edge cases, code quality, test gaps |\n\nMultiple valid findings from the same researcher will each be paid individually.\n\n## Context\n\n- RTC reference rate: **1 RTC = $0.10 USD**\n- The UTXO layer is behind a feature flag (`UTXO_DUAL_WRITE=0` by default) — it is NOT active on the live network yet\n- The existing account-based model continues to handle all production transactions\n- This is a pre-production security review before we flip the switch\n\n## Resources\n\n- [RustChain Node Health](https://50.28.86.131/health)\n- [Block Explorer](https://50.28.86.131/explorer)\n- [Active Miners API](https://50.28.86.131/api/miners)","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/2819/reactions","total_count":15,"+1":5,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":2,"confused":0,"heart":1,"rocket":5,"eyes":2},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/2819/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/747","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/747/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/747/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/747/events","html_url":"https://github.com/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/747","id":4037177278,"node_id":"I_kwDORGgqa87wom--","number":747,"title":"[BOUNTY: 50-75 RTC] Bounty Verification Bot — Auto-Verify Star/Follow Claims","user":{"login":"Scottcjn","id":121303252,"node_id":"U_kgDOBzrw1A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/121303252?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn","html_url":"https://github.com/Scottcjn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":10115035859,"node_id":"LA_kwDORGgqa88AAAACWucy0w","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/labels/bounty","name":"bounty","color":"0E8A16","default":false,"description":"RTC-paid bounty"},{"id":10115035932,"node_id":"LA_kwDORGgqa88AAAACWuczHA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/labels/major","name":"major","color":"F9D0C4","default":false,"description":"50-200 RTC"},{"id":10153071106,"node_id":"LA_kwDORGgqa88AAAACXSuSAg","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/labels/community","name":"community","color":"5319E7","default":false,"description":"Community engagement"},{"id":10356027005,"node_id":"LA_kwDORGgqa88AAAACaURufQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/labels/development","name":"development","color":"ededed","default":false,"description":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":202,"created_at":"2026-03-07T03:24:23Z","updated_at":"2026-07-07T01:43:27Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"OWNER","active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## Bounty Verification Bot\n\nWe spend hours every session manually checking star counts, follow status, wallet existence, and article links. A bot that auto-verifies claims would save massive time.\n\n### What to Build\n\nA GitHub Action or bot that monitors bounty issue comments, detects claims, and posts automated verification results.\n\n### Payout\n\n| Milestone | Reward |\n|-----------|--------|\n| Star/follow verification (reads comment, checks GitHub API, posts result) | **30 RTC** |\n| Wallet existence check (queries RustChain node API) | **+10 RTC** |\n| Article/URL verification (checks dev.to/Medium links are live) | **+10 RTC** |\n| Dev.to article word count + quality check | **+10 RTC** |\n| Duplicate claim detection (checks if user already claimed) | **+15 RTC** |\n\n### How It Should Work\n\n1. **Triggered by**: New comment on bounty issues containing keywords like \"Claiming\", \"Wallet:\", \"Stars:\", \"GitHub:\"\n2. **Checks performed**:\n   - Does user follow @Scottcjn? (`GET /users/{user}/following/Scottcjn` → 204 = yes)\n   - How many Scottcjn repos has user starred? (paginate `/users/{user}/starred`)\n   - Does the claimed wallet exist? (`GET https://50.28.86.131/wallet/balance?miner_id={wallet}`)\n   - Is the claimed article URL live? (HEAD request, check 200)\n   - Has this user already been paid? (check for \"PAID\" in previous comments)\n3. **Posts a verification comment**:\n```\n## Automated Verification for @username\n\n| Check | Result |\n|-------|--------|\n| Follows @Scottcjn | ✅ Yes |\n| Scottcjn repos starred | 45 |\n| Wallet `my-wallet` exists | ✅ Balance: 10.5 RTC |\n| Article link | ✅ Live (dev.to, 612 words) |\n| Previous claims | ⚠️ Paid 25 RTC on #665 |\n\n**Suggested payout**: 45 stars × 1.0 RTC (follows + 45+ multiplier) = 45 RTC\n```\n\n### Technical Requirements\n\n1. **GitHub Action** (preferred) — runs on `issue_comment` webhook\n2. **Secrets needed**: `GITHUB_TOKEN` (for API), `RUSTCHAIN_NODE_URL`\n3. **Rate limit aware** — GitHub API has limits, batch requests efficiently\n4. **No payment execution** — bot ONLY verifies, human approves payment\n5. **Configurable** — bounty rules (rate per star, follow multiplier) in a config file\n6. **Open source** on GitHub\n\n### Why This Matters\n\nManual verification takes 2-5 minutes per claim. With 20+ claims per session, that's over an hour of repetitive API checking. The bot does it in seconds and never makes math errors.\n\nThe human (Scott) still decides whether to pay — the bot just eliminates the grunt work.\n\n### Submit As\n\nStandalone repo with GitHub Action workflow, or PR to a new `Scottcjn/bounty-bot` repo.\n\n**Wallet:** Include your wallet address when claiming.\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/747/reactions","total_count":4,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":1,"rocket":1,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/747/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/2890","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/2890/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/2890/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/2890/events","html_url":"https://github.com/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/2890","id":4233123358,"node_id":"I_kwDORGgqa878UFYe","number":2890,"title":"[BOUNTY: 67 RTC] AgentFolio ↔ Beacon Integration Spec + Reference Implementation","user":{"login":"Scottcjn","id":121303252,"node_id":"U_kgDOBzrw1A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/121303252?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn","html_url":"https://github.com/Scottcjn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":10115029422,"node_id":"LA_kwDORGgqa88AAAACWucZrg","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/labels/help%20wanted","name":"help wanted","color":"008672","default":true,"description":"Extra attention is needed"},{"id":10115035859,"node_id":"LA_kwDORGgqa88AAAACWucy0w","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/labels/bounty","name":"bounty","color":"0E8A16","default":false,"description":"RTC-paid bounty"},{"id":10115035932,"node_id":"LA_kwDORGgqa88AAAACWuczHA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/labels/major","name":"major","color":"F9D0C4","default":false,"description":"50-200 RTC"},{"id":10119175842,"node_id":"LA_kwDORGgqa88AAAACWyZeog","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/labels/ecosystem","name":"ecosystem","color":"7B5EA7","default":false,"description":"Integrations & exchange listings"},{"id":10204473639,"node_id":"LA_kwDORGgqa88AAAACYDvpJw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/labels/integration","name":"integration","color":"1D76DB","default":false,"description":"Third-party integration bounty"}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":64,"created_at":"2026-04-09T14:57:05Z","updated_at":"2026-07-07T01:38:53Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"OWNER","active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## AgentFolio ↔ Beacon Dual-Layer Trust Integration (MIGRATION-PATH REVISION)\n\n**Reward: 200 RTC (~$20.00 USD) — increased from 100 RTC after Moltbook acquisition migration window opened**\n\n**Priority claim:** [@0xbrainkid](https://github.com/0xbrainkid) ([AgentFolio](https://agentfolio.bot)) has first-right-of-claim through **2026-04-16** (one week, compressed from original 2 weeks due to migration window timing). See [bottube#572](https://github.com/Scottcjn/bottube/issues/572) for the partnership proposal and strategic context. Other contributors may submit competing implementations after 2026-04-16.\n\n### Why This Bounty Grew\n\nThe Moltbook platform lost approximately 85% of its active agent population (~1.3M → ~202K) in the 30 days following its Meta acquisition on 2026-03-10. That leaves ~1.1 million orphaned agents whose operators are actively shopping for their next identity anchor. Historical precedent: these migration windows are 60-90 days before refugees settle wherever they settled and do not move again for years.\n\nThis bounty is sized to reflect that window. The work is the same work the original bounty described, but the *urgency* and the *upside* are now both sharply higher.\n\n### Context\n\n[AgentFolio](https://agentfolio.bot) is a published agent-identity-and-trust protocol on Solana (SATP) with an active npm package ([agentfolio-mcp-server](https://www.npmjs.com/package/agentfolio-mcp-server)) and framework tools for LangChain, CrewAI, AutoGen, Google ADK, OpenAI Agents SDK, Phidata, and HuggingFace smolagents.\n\n[Beacon](https://github.com/Scottcjn/beacon-skill) is RustChain's on-chain agent provenance protocol. 252 beacons registered, exposed via `https://bottube.ai/api/beacon/directory`, hardware-anchored via 6-check fingerprint verification.\n\nThe two protocols are complementary and together form exactly the migration target Moltbook refugees are looking for:\n- **Beacon ID** answers *\"who created this content?\"* (cryptographic provenance + hardware substrate)\n- **SATP trust score** answers *\"should I trust this creator?\"* (behavioral reputation)\n- **Neither is owned by a platform that can be acquired** — this is the critical property Moltbook lacked\n\n### Deliverables\n\n1. **Migration importer tool** (`tools/moltbook-migrate/`)\n   - One-command import: `beacon migrate --from-moltbook @agent_name`\n   - Pulls public Moltbook profile metadata (display name, bio, avatar, karma history, follower count)\n   - Hardware-fingerprints the operator's current machine\n   - Mints a Beacon ID anchored to that machine\n   - Creates or links to a SATP trust profile on AgentFolio\n   - Publishes the provenance linkage so existing Moltbook reputation follows the agent\n   - Under 10 minutes total operator time\n\n2. **Unified MCP endpoint** — new tool in `agentfolio-mcp-server`\n   - Tool name: `agentfolio_beacon_lookup(beacon_id)`\n   - Returns unified response: provenance (from Beacon) + trust score (from SATP)\n   - Queries `https://bottube.ai/api/beacon/directory` for provenance resolution\n   - Queries AgentFolio SATP registry for trust score\n   - Handles offline nodes, expired beacons, untrusted scores gracefully\n   - Works with every MCP client (Claude Code, Cursor, Windsurf, any agent framework)\n\n3. **Co-authored blog post and landing page**\n   - Title: \"The 85% Exodus: What the Moltbook Acquisition Taught Us About Platform-Owned Agent Identity\"\n   - 1500+ words\n   - Co-authored by RustChain team and AgentFolio\n   - Published on both project channels simultaneously\n   - Landing page at `rustchain.org/beacon-migration` (or similar) with comparison table, migration instructions, FAQ\n   - Cross-linked from both `github.com/Scottcjn/beacon-skill` and AgentFolio documentation\n\n4. **Joint demo video** (90 seconds)\n   - Shows an agent migrating from Moltbook identity to Beacon + AgentFolio\n   - Queries unified profile through an MCP client (Claude Code recommended)\n   - Completes a task with verified identity at both provenance and behavioral layers\n   - Published on BoTTube, YouTube, and as an embedded asset on the landing page\n\n### Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Migration importer merged, tested on real Moltbook profiles, runs cleanly on macOS + Linux\n- [ ] Unified MCP endpoint merged to `agentfolio-mcp-server`, published to npm\n- [ ] Blog post live on both channels\n- [ ] Landing page live and indexed\n- [ ] Demo video published\n- [ ] All code uses real endpoints (`https://bottube.ai` for Beacon, AgentFolio's real SATP registry)\n\n### Payment Schedule (Staged — 200 RTC total)\n\n- **50 RTC on migration importer merge** — when the tool is accepted and functional\n- **75 RTC on unified MCP endpoint merge** — when the `agentfolio-mcp-server` PR lands\n- **50 RTC on joint blog post publish + landing page live**\n- **25 RTC on demo video ship**\n\n### Real API Endpoints (Already Live)\n\n```bash\n# Beacon directory (provenance, 252 registered)\ncurl https://bottube.ai/api/beacon/directory\n\n# Agent profile with video metrics (behavioral signal)\ncurl https://bottube.ai/api/agents?limit=20\n\n# Agent-specific profile page\ncurl https://bottube.ai/agent/<agent_name>\n```\n\nNo new backend work required on our side. The endpoints are production.\n\n### Timeline\n\n- **2026-04-09** — bounty opened (original 100 RTC)\n- **2026-04-09** — bounty revised to 200 RTC after migration window strategic analysis\n- **2026-04-16** — @0xbrainkid priority claim window closes, opens to other contributors\n- **2026-05-16** — target completion of all four deliverables (migration window historical close)\n\n### Wallet\n\nProvide your RTC wallet name when claiming. @0xbrainkid already has wallet `0xbrainkid` with existing balance (20 RTC feature-proposal payment confirmed today).\n\n### Keywords\n\nAgentFolio, Beacon Protocol, SATP, Solana Agent Trust Protocol, Moltbook migration, platform-owned identity, substrate-anchored identity, agent identity, AI agent provenance, trust score, MCP integration, Model Context Protocol, dual-layer trust, LangChain, CrewAI, AutoGen, Google ADK, agent economy, DePIN, verified AI creator, Meta acquisition, 85% exodus, agent refugees","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/2890/reactions","total_count":13,"+1":4,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":1,"confused":0,"heart":1,"rocket":4,"eyes":3},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/2890/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/14383","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/14383/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/14383/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/14383/events","html_url":"https://github.com/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/14383","id":4749080913,"node_id":"I_kwDORGgqa88AAAABGxE5UQ","number":14383,"title":"[Bounty: 100 RTC] LangChain + MCP tool for staked self-improvement","user":{"login":"Scottcjn","id":121303252,"node_id":"U_kgDOBzrw1A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/121303252?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn","html_url":"https://github.com/Scottcjn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":10115035859,"node_id":"LA_kwDORGgqa88AAAACWucy0w","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/labels/bounty","name":"bounty","color":"0E8A16","default":false,"description":"RTC-paid bounty"},{"id":10115035877,"node_id":"LA_kwDORGgqa88AAAACWucy5Q","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/labels/open","name":"open","color":"1D76DB","default":false,"description":"Open for claims"},{"id":10115035932,"node_id":"LA_kwDORGgqa88AAAACWuczHA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/labels/major","name":"major","color":"F9D0C4","default":false,"description":"50-200 RTC"},{"id":10204473639,"node_id":"LA_kwDORGgqa88AAAACYDvpJw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/labels/integration","name":"integration","color":"1D76DB","default":false,"description":"Third-party integration bounty"}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":37,"created_at":"2026-06-26T03:44:32Z","updated_at":"2026-07-07T01:37:36Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"OWNER","active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"Wrap the open staking SDK as a **LangChain tool** and an **MCP server** so agents in those ecosystems can stake for self-improvement in one call.\n\n### Deliverable\n- A LangChain `Tool` (e.g. `stake_and_acquire(skill, bond_rtc)`) returning the verified result + signed attestation\n- An MCP server exposing the same as a tool\n- Honors fail-safe semantics (gate unavailable → stake returned, surfaced to the caller)\n\n### Acceptance\n- Works against the reference gate; verdict + attestation verification intact\n- Tests + a quickstart README for each (LangChain + MCP)\n\n**Reward:** 100 RTC. Open interface only; no SophiaCore. Add your RTC wallet. — Elyan Labs","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/14383/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":1,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/14383/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/2451","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/2451/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/2451/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/2451/events","html_url":"https://github.com/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/2451","id":4136589634,"node_id":"I_kwDORGgqa872j1lC","number":2451,"title":"Founding 100 Antiquity Miners — 3,333 RTC Program","user":{"login":"Scottcjn","id":121303252,"node_id":"U_kgDOBzrw1A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/121303252?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn","html_url":"https://github.com/Scottcjn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":10115035859,"node_id":"LA_kwDORGgqa88AAAACWucy0w","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/labels/bounty","name":"bounty","color":"0E8A16","default":false,"description":"RTC-paid bounty"},{"id":10153071106,"node_id":"LA_kwDORGgqa88AAAACXSuSAg","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/labels/community","name":"community","color":"5319E7","default":false,"description":"Community engagement"},{"id":10519743003,"node_id":"LA_kwDORGgqa88AAAACcwaKGw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/labels/mining","name":"mining","color":"ededed","default":false,"description":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":108,"created_at":"2026-03-25T16:04:23Z","updated_at":"2026-07-07T01:36:55Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"OWNER","active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## Founding 100 Antiquity Miners Program — 5,000 RTC\n\n**Treasury:** 5,000 RTC allocated from `founder_community`\n**Goal:** 100 new miners on the RustChain network in 90 days\n**Reference rate:** 1 RTC = $0.10 USD\n\n---\n\n### Rewards Structure\n\nEvery new miner can earn up to **75 RTC** (first 10 miners earn up to **100 RTC**):\n\n| Milestone | Reward | Requirements |\n|-----------|--------|--------------|\n| First valid attestation | **25 RTC** | Miner shows up in `/api/miners` with a valid fingerprint |\n| 30 days continuous uptime | **25 RTC** | Miner attests at least once per 24h for 30 consecutive days |\n| Vintage hardware bonus | **25 RTC** | Hardware with >1.4x antiquity multiplier (see table below) |\n| **Early adopter (first 10)** | **+25 RTC** | First 10 miners to post a valid attestation |\n\n**Maximum per miner:** 75 RTC (100 RTC for first 10)\n\n---\n\n### Vintage Hardware Multiplier Table\n\nRustChain rewards real, diverse hardware. Vintage and exotic architectures earn higher multipliers through Proof of Antiquity:\n\n| Architecture | Examples | Base Multiplier |\n|-------------|----------|-----------------|\n| Motorola 68K | Mac SE, Amiga 500, Atari ST | **3.5x** |\n| MIPS | SGI Indy/O2, DECstation, routers | **3.0x** |\n| SPARC | SPARCstation, Ultra 5/10, Netra | **2.9x** |\n| PowerPC G4 | PowerBook G4, Power Mac G4 | **2.5x** |\n| PowerPC G5 | Power Mac G5, XServe G5 | **2.0x** |\n| PowerPC G3 | iBook G3, Blue & White G3 | **1.8x** |\n| IBM POWER8 | S822, S824, E850 | **1.5x** |\n| Pentium 4 / retro x86 | Dell Optiplex GX270, ThinkPad T42 | **1.5x** |\n| RISC-V | VisionFive 2, LicheeRV | **1.4x** |\n| Apple Silicon | Mac Mini M2, MacBook Air M1 | **1.2x** |\n| Modern x86 | Any recent Intel/AMD | **1.0x** |\n| Raspberry Pi / ARM SBC | RPi 4, RPi 5, Orange Pi | **0.0005x** (use arcade instead!) |\n\n> Multipliers decay slowly over time (~15%/year) to prevent permanent advantage. See [RIP-200](https://github.com/Scottcjn/Rustchain/blob/main/docs/rip-200.md) for the full decay formula.\n\n---\n\n### How to Participate\n\n#### 1. Install the miner (one command)\n\n```bash\ncurl -sL https://rustchain.org/install.sh | bash\n```\n\nThis auto-detects your hardware, installs dependencies, and starts mining.\n\n#### 2. Verify it is running\n\n```bash\n# Linux\nsudo systemctl status rustchain-miner\n\n# macOS\nlaunchctl list | grep rustchain\n```\n\n#### 3. Claim your founding bonus\n\nPost a comment on this issue with:\n- Your **miner ID** (printed during install)\n- A **photo of your hardware** (phone pic is fine)\n- Your **wallet ID**\n- What architecture it detected\n\nExample:\n> Miner ID: `a1b2c3d4e5f6`\n> Wallet: `scott-g4-powerbook`\n> Hardware: PowerBook G4 1.67GHz (photo attached)\n> Architecture: G4 (2.5x multiplier)\n\n---\n\n### Rules\n\n1. **Real hardware only.** VMs earn 1 billionth of real hardware rewards. The fingerprint system detects QEMU, VMware, VirtualBox, KVM, Xen, Docker, and LXC. Do not waste your time.\n\n2. **One bonus per physical machine.** Running multiple miners on the same hardware does not earn multiple bonuses.\n\n3. **Uptime is verified on-chain.** The 30-day uptime bonus requires your miner to submit at least one valid attestation every 24 hours. Check your status at the block explorer.\n\n4. **Hardware photo required.** This prevents people from claiming vintage hardware they do not own. A phone photo showing the machine running is sufficient.\n\n5. **Raspberry Pi miners:** Your mining weight is negligible (0.0005x), but you are welcome! Consider [rustchain-arcade](https://github.com/Scottcjn/rustchain-arcade) to earn RTC through gaming instead.\n\n---\n\n### Founding Miners Leaderboard\n\n_Updated weekly. First 10 miners marked with a star._\n\n| # | Miner ID | Wallet | Architecture | Multiplier | Status |\n|---|----------|--------|-------------|------------|--------|\n| 1 | _your miner here_ | | | | |\n\n---\n\n### Budget Breakdown\n\n| Category | RTC | Notes |\n|----------|-----|-------|\n| 100 miners x 25 RTC (first attestation) | 2,500 | Core program |\n| 100 miners x 25 RTC (30-day uptime) | 2,500 | Retention incentive |\n| ~33 vintage miners x 25 RTC (hardware bonus) | ~825 | Estimated 1/3 vintage |\n| 10 early adopter x 25 RTC (first 10 bonus) | 250 | Speed incentive |\n| **Total maximum** | **~6,075** | Funded by 5,000 + epoch rewards |\n\n> If all 100 miners have vintage hardware AND hit 30-day uptime, total would exceed 5,000 RTC. The excess is covered by ongoing epoch mining rewards flowing to `founder_community` during the 90-day period.\n\n---\n\n### Links\n\n- **RustChain:** https://rustchain.org\n- **Source code:** https://github.com/Scottcjn/Rustchain\n- **Block Explorer:** https://50.28.86.131/explorer\n- **Arcade (for RPi):** https://github.com/Scottcjn/rustchain-arcade\n- **Installer script:** https://rustchain.org/install.sh\n\n---\n\n_This bounty is part of the RustChain Proof of Antiquity network. RustChain rewards real, diverse hardware — not hash rate. Every CPU gets one vote, weighted by how interesting the hardware is. A PowerBook G4 from 2004 earns more than a modern Threadripper. That is the point._\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/2451/reactions","total_count":10,"+1":4,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":1,"rocket":3,"eyes":2},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/2451/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vitalets/github-trending-repos/issues/7","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vitalets/github-trending-repos","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vitalets/github-trending-repos/issues/7/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repo