r_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lcn2","html_url":"https://github.com/lcn2","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lcn2/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lcn2/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lcn2/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lcn2/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lcn2/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lcn2/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lcn2/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lcn2/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lcn2/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"Due to the fact that we have another issue that has had a number of OT comments I think it might be good to have a new mostly OT thread here rather than clutter the one in the other repo more or the issue for jprint.\r\n\r\nI had the thought of suggesting you reopen the other one but there's a comment there I don't want to get lost that I hope you can finish replying to (you were doing it in parts) when things are less busy here. I also wanted to see if anything in particular occurs if one uses the same name (I rather doubt it will but it popped into my head anyway).\r\n\r\nFeel free to assign this to me even though it's not technically an issue that has to be resolved.","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioccc-src/mkiocccentry/issues/723/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioccc-src/mkiocccentry/issues/723/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ValveSoftware/Proton/issues/7199","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ValveSoftware/Proton","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ValveSoftware/Proton/issues/7199/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ValveSoftware/Proton/issues/7199/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ValveSoftware/Proton/issues/7199/events","html_url":"https://github.com/ValveSoftware/Proton/issues/7199","id":1961939568,"node_id":"I_kwDOB3TbgM508NJw","number":7199,"title":"Diablo IV (2344520)","user":{"login":"christofin","id":43354771,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQzMzU0Nzcx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/43354771?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/christofin","html_url":"https://github.com/christofin","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/christofin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/christofin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/christofin/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/christofin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/christofin/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/christofin/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/christofin/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/christofin/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/christofin/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":1032039901,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxMDMyMDM5OTAx","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ValveSoftware/Proton/labels/Game%20compatibility%20-%20Unofficial","name":"Game compatibility - Unofficial","color":"ea6e3c","default":false,"description":"Games not expected to work without issues"},{"id":1041498223,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxMDQxNDk4MjIz","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ValveSoftware/Proton/labels/Regression","name":"Regression","color":"b60205","default":false,"description":"Confirmed working on an older version of Proton"}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":77,"created_at":"2023-10-25T17:54:53Z","updated_at":"2026-07-06T23:34:20Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"# Compatibility Report\r\n- Name of the game with compatibility issues: Diablo IV\r\n- Steam AppID of the game: 2344520\r\n\r\n## System Information\r\nSteam Deck - latest full 3.4.x release (NOT 3.5.1 preview)\r\n- Proton version: Proton Experimental - set by Valve in Game Properties (as of 10/25/2023)\r\n\r\n## I confirm:\r\n- [X] that I haven't found an existing compatibility report for this game.\r\n- [X] that I have checked whether there are updates for my system available.\r\n\r\n<!-- Please add `PROTON_LOG=1 %command%` to the game's launch options and\r\nattach the generated $HOME/steam-$APPID.log to this issue report as a file.\r\n(Proton logs compress well if needed.)-->\r\n\r\n## Symptoms: <!-- What's the problem? -->\r\nDiablo IV fails to reconnect to Blizzard servers after using the sleep/wake function. I'm not sure if this is a game issue or Proton, but the sleep/wake function on Playstation and Xbox work, so I'm reporting here for awareness. \r\n\r\n\r\n## Reproduction\r\n\r\nLaunch Diablo IV on Steam Deck\r\nConnect to Blizzard Servers, load into game after character select\r\nPut Steam Deck to Sleep\r\nWake Steam Deck back up\r\nYour character is still in the world, with \"Connecting to Diablo IV Servers\" in the upper left corner\r\nGame will fail to connect to Diablo IV servers, returns player to main menu\r\nGame fails to connect to Diablo IV servers in main menu, application exits to desktop\r\n\r\nExpected behavior is for the game to successfully reconnect to Blizzard servers and allow player to resume gameplay. \r\n\r\nNote that in a normal scenario (e.g. on Playstation and Xbox), any server or client related hotfixes or patches will result in showing the player an error and exit the application. This is normal behavior when there is a server & client mismatch. The issue I am describing here is NOT a result of server/client mismatch. This issue is reproducible 100% of the time, even when using the sleep function very briefly (e.g. under 2 minutes). ","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ValveSoftware/Proton/issues/7199/reactions","total_count":5,"+1":5,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ValveSoftware/Proton/issues/7199/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Expensify/App/issues/94758","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Expensify/App","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Expensify/App/issues/94758/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Expensify/App/issues/94758/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Expensify/App/issues/94758/events","html_url":"https://github.com/Expensify/App/issues/94758","id":4756729209,"node_id":"I_kwDOEQqHYc8AAAABG4XteQ","number":94758,"title":"[$250] Workflows - Approval Workflow lags and UI breaks after navigating back","user":{"login":"applause-bot[bot]","id":265651874,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOD9WGog","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/3009811?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/applause-bot%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/applause-bot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/applause-bot%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/applause-bot%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"ht