eceived_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"parent_issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Expensify/App/issues/91302","issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## Sentry\nhttps://expensify.sentry.io/issues/APP-25V\n\n## Impact (snapshot at filing)\n- Users (total since first seen): **1,938**\n- Events: 4,178\n- Users (last 14d, releases 9.3.89–9.3.91): 3\n- First seen: 2025-12-05\n- Last seen: now (ongoing)\n- Platform: iOS, hybrid_app\n- App version(s): seen on 9.3.59 through 9.3.91\n- Mechanism: `mach`, fatal\n\n## Stack trace (top frames, first-party only)\n```\nfacebook::react::RuntimeScheduler_Modern::runEventLoopTick\n  -> facebook::react::RuntimeScheduler_Modern::runEventLoop\n  -> facebook::react::RCTMessageThread::runAsync\n  -> RCT JSThread run loop\n```\n\n## Suspected cause\nRN Fabric/modern scheduler memory corruption or use-after-free on the JS thread during an event-loop tick. Stack is native-only (no app JS frames), so the fix may require a React Native upgrade or platform-team investigation.\n\n## Reproduction\nUnknown deterministically — fires on the RN JS thread under load on HybridApp iOS. See linked Sentry events.\n\n## Related\n- Sibling Sentry IDs (if any): none identified\n- Prior GH issues: none\n- Production scan: releases 9.3.89, 9.3.90, 9.3.91 (2026-06-02)\n\n<details><summary>Upwork Automation - Do Not Edit</summary>\n    <ul>\n        <li>Upwork Job URL: <a href=\"https://www.upwork.com/jobs/~022061885259834583946\">https://www.upwork.com/jobs/~022061885259834583946</a></li>\n        <li>Upwork Job ID: 2061885259834583946</li>\n        <li>Last Price Increase: 2026-06-16</li>\n    </ul>\n</details>\n\n<details><summary>Issue Owner</summary>Current Issue Owner: @mallenexpensify</details>","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Expensify/App/issues/92412/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Expensify/App/issues/92412/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ethereum/ethereum-org-website/issues/18433","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ethereum/ethereum-org-website","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ethereum/ethereum-org-website/issues/18433/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ethereum/ethereum-org-website/issues/18433/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ethereum/ethereum-org-website/issues/18433/events","html_url":"https://github.com/ethereum/ethereum-org-website/issues/18433","id":4699525714,"node_id":"I_kwDOBvEA_s8AAAABGB0SUg","number":18433,"title":"Suggest a staking product or service","user":{"login":"luganodes-visvesh","id":294104015,"node_id":"U_kgDOEYerzw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/294104015?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/luganodes-visvesh","html_url":"https://github.com/luganodes-visvesh","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luganodes-visvesh/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luganodes-visvesh/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luganodes-visvesh/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luganodes-visvesh/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luganodes-visvesh/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luganodes-visvesh/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luganodes-visvesh/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luganodes-visvesh/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luganodes-visvesh/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":6799206342,"node_id":"LA_kwDOBvEA_s8AAAABlUOnxg","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ethereum/ethereum-org-website/labels/product%20%F0%9F%A7%B0","name":"product 🧰","color":"fef2c0","default":false,"description":"This involves a product listing"}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":1,"created_at":"2026-06-19T09:22:06Z","updated_at":"2026-07-06T21:14:16Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Project name\n\nLuganodes\n\n### Product type\n\nStaking as a service\n\n### If other product type, please describe\n\nInstitutional-Grade, also an RPC provider\n\n### Logo\n\n<img width=\"1209\" height=\"678\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/b23e57e3-ae89-47e2-8b74-9bf6d03fa861\" />\n\n### Description\n\nLuganodes is a world-class, non-custodial blockchain infrastructure provider, securing $2B+ in staked assets, tailored for institutions. Operating across 40+ PoS networks, 50+ institutional clients, Luganodes maintains 99.9% uptime, with an emphasis on security and compliance.\n\n### Website\n\nwww.luganodes.com\n\n### If software is involved, is everything open source?\n\nPortions of code are open source: provide link(s) to project repo(s)\n\n### Is the project a fork? If yes, which project was forked?\n\nNo\n\n### Is the product out of beta development?\n\nYes product is out of beta development and we have live customers as well\nWe have a batch contract \nWe have built open source tool for batch consolidation\nhttps://github.com/Luganodes/Pectra-Batch-Contract\nhttps://github.com/Luganodes/pectra-cli\nthe batch deposit contract is forked\nExit functionality on Api utilises a striped down version of the staking deposit cli\n\n### What wallets support the product or service?\n\nIntegrated with WalletConnect so support the 520+ wallets connected with WalletConnect\n\n### If the product or service enables staking with <32 ETH, what is the minimum ETH required to stake?\n\nNative staking does not allow below 32 ETH (Min 32)\nPooled staking offering allows below 32 ETH\nETH pooled staking enabled via stakewise no minimum ETH requirements \nNo staking requirements as such\n\n### If a service, what are the fees associated with using the service?\n\nmonthly commission on earning\nbased on tiered approach on the amount being staked (varies from client to client)\nInflationary rewards from staking\n\n\n### If the product or service involved a liquidity token, what are the tokens involved?\n\nno liquidity token involved\n\n### What date did the project or service go live?\n\nHave been live since Q4 2022 Ethereum staking services started Q3 2023 https://explorer.rated.network/o/Luganodes\n\n### Has the project undergone an external security audit?\n\nNo \nWe are undergoing Audit from Quantstamp\n\n\n### Has the project undergone any security bug bounties?\n\nNo\n\n### Is the project being actively maintained?\n\nYes\n\n### Is the product or service free of trusted/human intermediaries?\n\nNo we perform KYC for institutional clients\nWe do not have keys that needed to be trusted with humans\nBut after Pectra the private key of the withdrawal address is managed by the client always and we do not have access to it\nWithdrawal address is managed by the client always so we do not have access to it\n\n\n### If a pooled staking service, can users participate as a node operator without permission?\n\nWe have a pooled staking service offering\nUsers cannot operate as a node operator even if applying for pooled staking\nStaking to the already existing node is permissionless\n\n\n### If listing a staking-as-a-service, are users required to sign-up for an account?\n\nYes account needed for dApp\nAccount needed for API(and API key)\ndApp requires Wallet login and normal login\n\n\n### If listing as staking-as-a-service, who has access to the signing keys?\n\nWe solely have custody of the validator signing keys, Withdrawal address access remains with user/clients only.\n\n### If a pooled staking service or SaaS provider, what type of withdrawal credentials are being utilized / who holds the withdrawal keys?\n\nIn cases of SaaS we use both(0x01 and 0x02) depending on user request (chosen by the user)\nWe hold the keystore and mnemonic and client holds the withdrawal address\nIn case of pooled staking it’s a smart contract (using Stakewise vaults)\nWithdrawal account chosen by the user\n\n### If a pooled staking service or SaaS provider, what percent of node operators are running a super-majority client?\n\n100% on CL AND equal share on EL(Validator can choose any EL client)\nOn Consensus no diversity only Lighthouse on EL we use Reth Nethermind Geth\nNo Super majority\n\n\n### If listing node or client tooling, which consensus layer clients (Lighthouse, Teku, Nimbus, or Prysm) are supported?\n\nLighthouse is supported \nthere are no other options to switch\n\n### What platforms are supported?\n\nWebsite GUI\n\n### What user interfaces are supported?\n\nBrowser app we have REST APIs and Website GUI\n\n### Social media links\n\nTwitter/X: https://x.com/luganodes\nLinkedIn: https://www.linkedin.com/company/luganodes\nYoutube: https://www.youtube.com/@luganodes\n\n### Would you like to work on this issue?\n\n- [ ] Yes\n- [ ] No","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ethereum/ethereum-org-website/issues/18433/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ethereum/ethereum-org-website/issues/18433/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/r