ropean Organisation for Astronomical Research in the Southern Hemisphere\n\n  </details>\n\n  [eso.org](https://www.eso.org/public/news/eso2607/) | 114 points by [Breadmaker](https://news.ycombinator.com/user?id=Breadmaker) at 01:17:28 | [203 comments](https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=48787042)\n\n\n  <details>\n    <summary>\n      <strong>Wicklow hotel cancels &#39;secretive&#39; Peter Thiel group conference</strong>\n    </summary>\n\nPowerscourt Hotel and Spa event was to be hosted by Dialog and attended by senior Nato commander and Trump administration officials\n\n  </details>\n\n  [irishtimes.com](https://www.irishtimes.com/ireland/2026/07/03/wicklow-hotel-cancels-secretive-peter-thiel-conference/) | 114 points by [01-_-](https://news.ycombinator.com/user?id=01-_-) at 03:08:44 | [43 comments](https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=48787987)\n\n\n  <details>\n    <summary>\n      <strong>Programmers need to start meditating</strong>\n    </summary>\n\nFor over 20 years, the meditative focus of programming has been one of the best parts of my job.\nEvery week I&rsquo;d spend countless hours in a flow state, which quiets the default mode network. The DMN is responsible for daydreaming/reflection but also rumination/worrying, so quieting it settles your mind. If I didn&rsquo;t manage to write code for a week, I&rsquo;d start to notice it.\nNow it&rsquo;s context switching all day\nI&rsquo;m clearly much more productive now. I&rsquo;m doing five things at once very effectively, switching between multiple agent sessions from morning to night. After working full-time like this for ~8 months, one thing I&rsquo;m sure of is that this way of working involves much less time spent in a flow state.\n\n  </details>\n\n  [jacob.gold](https://jacob.gold/posts/programmers-need-to-start-meditating-now/) | 112 points by [enz](https://news.ycombinator.com/user?id=enz) at 15:39:35 | [122 comments](https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=48792080)\n\n\n  <details>\n    <summary>\n 